import{_ as t,o as i,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 620 | Time Domain and Civilizational Institutions | Anchor-Supervisory-Committee Audit of the Time Domain","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 620 | Time Domain and Civilizational Institutions | Anchor-Supervisory-Committee Audit of the Time Domain","no":620,"module":3,"tags":["Time Domain","Anchor Supervisory Committee","Audit","Supervision","Civilizational Institution"],"related":["49-Governance Framework and Power Checks","29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System","27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0620_模块3-时间域文明制度-锚点监督委员会审计.md","filePath":"en/0620_模块3-时间域文明制度-锚点监督委员会审计.md"}'),n={name:"en/0620_模块3-时间域文明制度-锚点监督委员会审计.md"};function r(s,e,l,u,d,h){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-620-time-domain-and-civilizational-institutions-anchor-supervisory-committee-audit-of-the-time-domain" tabindex="-1">Entry 620 | Time Domain and Civilizational Institutions | Anchor-Supervisory-Committee Audit of the Time Domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-620-time-domain-and-civilizational-institutions-anchor-supervisory-committee-audit-of-the-time-domain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 620 | Time Domain and Civilizational Institutions | Anchor-Supervisory-Committee Audit of the Time Domain&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 49, 29, 27 | Series: Time Domain and Civilizational Institutions (Entry 5)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-legislature-executive-judiciary-all-in-place-—-who-watches-the-three" tabindex="-1">Introduction: legislature, executive, judiciary all in place — who watches the three <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-legislature-executive-judiciary-all-in-place-—-who-watches-the-three" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: legislature, executive, judiciary all in place — who watches the three&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Anchor Council legislates (Entry 618), the Symbiotic Executive Committee enforces, the symbiotic court adjudicates (Entry 619). Separation of powers looks complete. But separation itself can go wrong — legislators partial, executives lax, judiciary corrupt. So a fourth power is needed: the independent audit of the <strong>Anchor Supervisory Committee</strong>. This entry tells how the Supervisory Committee audits every operation of the time domain, making &quot;no one is an exception&quot; real.</p><p>Six top-level axioms are audit&#39;s yardstick: anti-predation axiom is audit&#39;s red line; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires audit open to Myriad Ranks; collective ascension axiom requires audit drive improvement not targeting people; causal self-discipline axiom requires audit trace-through; law-first axiom requires audit standards stable, not stretching by the auditor&#39;s taste. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-what-to-audit-three-tables" tabindex="-1">I. What to Audit: Three Tables <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-what-to-audit-three-tables" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. What to Audit: Three Tables&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Anchor Supervisory Committee regularly audits three tables of the time domain:</p><ol><li><strong>Allocation table</strong>: against Entry 616 joint-contracting rules, review whether acceleration time is truly allocated by contribution, whether strong ones crowd out, whether contribution is forged.</li><li><strong>Feedback table</strong>: against Entry 614 access protocol, review whether domain-internal outputs truly feed back to the Alaya Network, whether privately retained, whether smuggled un-desensitized causality.</li><li><strong>Energy-consumption table</strong>: against Entry 613 energy engineering, review whether energy收支 is incrementally positive, whether under the name of R&amp;D extraction is being done.</li></ol><p>Three tables correspond to &quot;allocation fair, outputs public, energy incremental&quot; three vital points.</p><h2 id="ii-how-to-audit-independent-through-out" tabindex="-1">II. How to Audit: Independent + Through-Out <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-how-to-audit-independent-through-out" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. How to Audit: Independent + Through-Out&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Supervisory Committee&#39;s audit has two features:</p><ul><li><strong>Independence</strong>: the Committee does not belong to the Council or Executive Committee, directly responsible to Myriad Ranks, ensuring audit is not interfered with by the audited.</li><li><strong>Through-out</strong>: Alaya Network data is audit&#39;s factual basis (Entry 615); the Committee pulls all timestamps, causal accounts, feedback records, does not accept &quot;inconvenient to check.&quot;</li></ul><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Audited Object</th><th>Routine Frequency</th><th>Triggered Audit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ordinary cultivators</td><td>Sampling</td><td>On report or data anomaly</td></tr><tr><td>Executive Committee</td><td>Quarterly</td><td>After major accidents</td></tr><tr><td>Council legislation</td><td>Annual</td><td>On law revision</td></tr><tr><td>Transcendent-strength</td><td>Case-by-case</td><td>Linked to four-dimensional assessment (Document 17)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Audit&#39;s edge <strong>has no ceiling above, no floor below</strong> — including auditing legislators themselves.</p><h2 id="iii-audit-output-reports-and-rectification" tabindex="-1">III. Audit Output: Reports and Rectification <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-audit-output-reports-and-rectification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Audit Output: Reports and Rectification&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Audit is not going through the motions; its output is <strong>audit report + rectification order</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Report public</strong>: each audit produces a report, desensitized then network-wide published, Myriad Ranks may query.</li><li><strong>Rectification order</strong>: on finding problems, issue time-limited rectification order to the audited unit, and track re-inspection.</li><li><strong>Judicial referral</strong>: finding suspected Entry 619 four-category crimes, refer to the symbiotic court.</li><li><strong>Improvement feedback</strong>: feed institutional loopholes back to the Council, drive law amendment — audit is also an input to institutional evolution.</li></ul><p>Audit&#39;s final purpose is not targeting people, but making the time-domain system <strong>rotate cleaner and fairer</strong>.</p><h2 id="iv-supervision-of-the-supervisory-committee" tabindex="-1">IV. Supervision of the Supervisory Committee <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-supervision-of-the-supervisory-committee" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Supervision of the Supervisory Committee&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A sharp question: who supervises the supervisor? Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is <strong>dual-layer supervision</strong>:</p><ul><li>The Committee&#39;s own audit behavior is also recorded on the Alaya Network, may be pulled and reviewed by the Council.</li><li>Committee members&#39; appointment and removal involves Myriad-Rank representatives, not self-appointed.</li><li>If the Committee itself is corrupt, it too is tried by the symbiotic court — auditors breaking the law, crime adds one grade.</li></ul><p>This avoids the trap of &quot;supervisors becoming a new privileged class.&quot;</p><h2 id="supplementary-argument-supervision-keeps-the-system-from-becoming-what-it-hates" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Argument: Supervision Keeps the System From Becoming What It Hates <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-argument-supervision-keeps-the-system-from-becoming-what-it-hates" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Argument: Supervision Keeps the System From Becoming What It Hates&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Any institution operating long risks sliding toward vested interests — legislators enrich themselves, executives go lax, judiciary corrupts. The Anchor Supervisory Committee&#39;s existence is like installing a never-closed mirror on the time-domain system. It regularly reflects out whether allocation has been manipulated, whether feedback has been intercepted, whether energy has been falsified. More critically, this mirror also reflects the supervisors: if supervisors are corrupt, they too are tried. This dual-layer design of &quot;supervised are also supervised&quot; eliminates the birth of a new privileged class. Civilization&#39;s trust in the time domain ultimately does not come from how well it legislated, but from whether someone is truly watching — and watching the watchers.</p><h2 id="brief-transition" tabindex="-1">Brief Transition <a class="header-anchor" href="#brief-transition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Brief Transition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Committee&#39;s three tables likewise cover the Quest Sediment Domain: whether course allocation is fair, whether trial outputs are fed back, whether psychological assessment has become formalism. The Origin Acceleration Domain&#39;s time share and Quest Sediment Domain&#39;s trial quotas sit together on the same audit checklist, backed by the Alaya Network&#39;s public data.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: three-table audit catches idling, crowding, private retention, redirecting time resources to efficient places</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: allocation and feedback tables are the audit-ization of anti-predation axiom; plunder cannot hide</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo has no supervision, strong ones enrich themselves; Heng Yuan Zhou audits even transcendent-strength, no exception before law</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: audit reports public to Myriad Ranks; any clan finding unfairness may report or appeal</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: audit standards, report templates public; newly merged planes bring their own &quot;fourth power&quot; when接入</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The time-domain system&#39;s credibility lies not in how well it legislated, but in whether someone truly watches. The Anchor Supervisory Committee, with independent, through-out, public audit, adds another lock on the three powers of legislature, executive, judiciary. When &quot;anyone may be audited, audit reports network-wide queryable&quot; becomes normal, the time domain truly turns from &quot;strong ones&#39; toy&quot; into &quot;Myriad Ranks&#39; public asset.&quot;</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">Entry 49 · Governance Framework and Power Checks</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a> · <a href="./618_模块3-时间域文明制度-锚点议事会立法.html">Entry 618 · Anchor-Council Legislation</a> · <a href="./619_模块3-时间域文明制度-滥用共生法院审判.html">Entry 619 · Abuse Adjudication</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const p=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
